  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe utilizes 2 (2-compartment) food storage containers.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce. (Skip the mixed greens if they came pre-washed.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "¼ small bunch fresh dill\n1 medium carrot\n¼ (5 oz) pkg spring mix (mixed greens)\n1 (16 oz) pkg strawberries"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Drain and rinse chickpeas. Place in a medium bowl along with mayo, Dijon, vinegar, and spices. Use a fork or potato masher to crush the chickpeas, making a semi-smooth spread.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (15 oz) can garbanzo beans (chickpeas)\nmayonnaise\n1 tsp Dijon mustard\n1 tsp apple cider vinegar\n¼ tsp onion powder\n¼ tsp paprika\n¼ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Shave dill leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves. Add to the bowl and stir to combine the chickpea salad. Set aside.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel, trim, and coarsely grate carrot. Slice tomatoes crosswise, then using a paper towel, pat tomato slices on both sides to remove excess liquid (this will help keep the sandwiches from getting soggy).\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place bread slices on a flat surface. Spread half of the slices with a thick layer of chickpea salad, then top with carrot, tomato, and mixed greens. Spread remaining slices with a thin layer of mayo and close the sandwiches. Cut sandwiches in half (if desired) and wrap in parchment paper or plastic wrap to secure and maintain freshness.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "4 slice white bread\n2 tsp mayonnaise"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Divide sandwiches and strawberries between storage containers, cover, and refrigerate until ready to eat. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
